      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.67,
          "end": 4.56,
          "en": "-: So in the last lectures we learned a lot about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.56,
          "end": 8.79,
          "en": "the creation and configuration and usage of our own forms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.79,
          "end": 11.49,
          "en": "Now let's use another cool feature we can easily",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.49,
          "end": 13.89,
          "en": "implement when using the reactive approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.89,
          "end": 15.81,
          "en": "Adding our own validators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.81,
          "end": 18,
          "en": "Thus far we always use to build in ones.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18,
          "end": 20.79,
          "en": "And to be honest, with all the built in ones",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.79,
          "end": 24.39,
          "en": "you should be able to cover most of your use cases.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.39,
          "end": 26.76,
          "en": "But let's say we have some usernames you don't",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.76,
          "end": 29.28,
          "en": "want to allow the user to use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.28,
          "end": 33.3,
          "en": "In this case I'll go to my TypeScript file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.3,
          "end": 35.76,
          "en": "and here I'll add a new property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.76,
          "end": 38.7,
          "en": "for forbidden usernames for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.7,
          "end": 43.7,
          "en": "And in this array I'll add Chris and Anna",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.37,
          "end": 46.54,
          "en": "as forbidden usernames",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.33,
          "end": 49.95,
          "en": "if written like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.95,
          "end": 52.02,
          "en": "So now I want to create my own validator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.02,
          "end": 55.77,
          "en": "which checks whether the username the user entered is one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.77,
          "end": 58.86,
          "en": "of the two usernames specified here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.86,
          "end": 61.92,
          "en": "Now a new validator can be added pretty easily.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.92,
          "end": 64.65,
          "en": "A validator in the end is just a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.65,
          "end": 67.17,
          "en": "which gets executed by angular automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.17,
          "end": 69.87,
          "en": "when it checks the validity of the form control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.87,
          "end": 71.85,
          "en": "and it checks that validity",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.85,
          "end": 73.92,
          "en": "whenever you change that control.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.92,
          "end": 76.98,
          "en": "So a validator is just a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.98,
          "end": 80.35,
          "en": "Let's name it forbidden",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.81,
          "end": 82.743,
          "en": "names.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.88,
          "end": 86.82,
          "en": "Now a validator to work correctly needs to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.82,
          "end": 88.77,
          "en": "receive an argument which is to control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.77,
          "end": 90.06,
          "en": "it should check.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.06,
          "end": 93.24000000000001,
          "en": "So this will be of type form control.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.24000000000001,
          "end": 96.06,
          "en": "A validator also needs to return something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.06,
          "end": 99.72,
          "en": "for angular to be able to handle the return value correctly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.72,
          "end": 103.11,
          "en": "There's something should be a JavaScript object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.11,
          "end": 106.32,
          "en": "And now the following notation might look strange.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.32,
          "end": 111.03,
          "en": "It should have any key which can be interpreted as a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.03,
          "end": 113.34,
          "en": "And this is just types of syntax for saying,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.34,
          "end": 115.77000000000001,
          "en": "hey, we want to have a key value pair where the key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.77000000000001,
          "end": 118.77000000000001,
          "en": "again can be interpreted as a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 118.77000000000001,
          "end": 122.34,
          "en": "which is true for a key in an object in general.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 122.34,
          "end": 124.59,
          "en": "More importantly, the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 124.59,
          "end": 128.91,
          "en": "of that key key value pair that should be a boolean.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.91,
          "end": 132.45,
          "en": "So this function here should return something like",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 132.45,
          "end": 134.41,
          "en": "let's say an object where we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.51,
          "end": 138.57,
          "en": "name is forbidden.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 138.57,
          "end": 141.09,
          "en": "This would be the key name which is interpreted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 141.09,
          "end": 144.27,
          "en": "as a string and it could be true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 144.27,
          "end": 146.28,
          "en": "So this is what this function should return in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 146.28,
          "end": 149.77,
          "en": "For example, the message itself, the key name is up to us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 150.69,
          "end": 155.25,
          "en": "and therefore we can now add the logic in this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.25,
          "end": 158.13,
          "en": "In our case here, I want to check if the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.13,
          "end": 162.24,
          "en": "of the control is part of this forbidden user names array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162.24,
          "end": 167.22,
          "en": "So I want to check if this forbidden user names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.22,
          "end": 168.09,
          "en": "index off.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 168.09,
          "end": 170.57999999999998,
          "en": "So if it contains a certain element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 170.57999999999998,
          "end": 173.61,
          "en": "and the element is the value of our control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 173.61,
          "end": 176.76,
          "en": "we pass here the control we're checking.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 176.76,
          "end": 178.29,
          "en": "If this is the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 178.29,
          "end": 180.72,
          "en": "I want to return an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 180.72,
          "end": 181.84,
          "en": "where I say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 182.79,
          "end": 185.55,
          "en": "name is forbidden.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 185.55,
          "end": 190.383,
          "en": "Any short error code you want is true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 191.52,
          "end": 192.607,
          "en": "Now in the other case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.59,
          "end": 195,
          "en": "I want to return null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 195,
          "end": 196.92000000000002,
          "en": "And now this is important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 196.92000000000002,
          "end": 199.98,
          "en": "If validation is successful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 199.98,
          "end": 202.95,
          "en": "you have to pass nothing or null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 202.95,
          "end": 207.95,
          "en": "You should not pass this object with false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 208.2,
          "end": 210.21,
          "en": "This might sound counterintuitive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 210.21,
          "end": 212.19,
          "en": "but that's just how it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 212.19,
          "end": 216.81,
          "en": "It should be null or you simply omit the return statement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 216.81,
          "end": 221.76,
          "en": "This is how you tell Angler that the form control is valid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 221.76,
          "end": 225.96,
          "en": "Well, and this is all we created our own form validator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 225.96,
          "end": 227.79,
          "en": "or own validator here, important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 227.79,
          "end": 231.42000000000002,
          "en": "It receives the control and it returns this object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 231.42000000000002,
          "end": 234.69,
          "en": "with a arrow code and then true, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 234.69,
          "end": 236.37,
          "en": "if it is invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 236.37,
          "end": 239.79,
          "en": "So now to add this, I will go to my username",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 239.79,
          "end": 243.15,
          "en": "and actually we now want to assign an array of validators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 243.15,
          "end": 245.67,
          "en": "So I'll change this appropriately",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 245.67,
          "end": 250.41,
          "en": "and I'll now add a reference to my forbidden names function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 250.41,
          "end": 253.92,
          "en": "Again, don't execute it, only pass a reference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 253.92,
          "end": 257.79,
          "en": "And now if we save this, we get an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 257.79,
          "end": 260.13,
          "en": "Now this can be a tough one to spot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 260.13,
          "end": 261.753,
          "en": "What's going wrong here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 262.8,
          "end": 264.3,
          "en": "This error has something to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 264.3,
          "end": 267.24,
          "en": "with the way JavaScript handles this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 267.24,
          "end": 272.15999999999997,
          "en": "In forbidden names I'm accessing this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 272.15999999999997,
          "end": 274.08,
          "en": "Now this might look all right because I'm",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 274.08,
          "end": 278.82,
          "en": "in this class and I access this forbidden user names.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 278.82,
          "end": 283.32,
          "en": "But think about who is calling this forbidden names.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 283.32,
          "end": 286.08,
          "en": "We're not calling it from inside this class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 286.08,
          "end": 289.62,
          "en": "Angler will call it when it checks the validity.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 289.62,
          "end": 291.18,
          "en": "At this point of time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 291.18,
          "end": 294.84000000000003,
          "en": "this will not refer to our class here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 294.84000000000003,
          "end": 299.82,
          "en": "So to fix this, I actually need to bind this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 299.82,
          "end": 303.6,
          "en": "the good old JavaScript trick to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 303.6,
          "end": 307.95,
          "en": "that this refers to what we want it to refer to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 307.95,
          "end": 310.2,
          "en": "So with this in place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 310.2,
          "end": 313.77,
          "en": "if we now let this recompile, the error is gone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 313.77,
          "end": 315.93,
          "en": "Let's now check the validity of this input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 315.93,
          "end": 319.44,
          "en": "Here it is invalid, but if I under test here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 319.44,
          "end": 320.883,
          "en": "it stays invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 321.96,
          "end": 324.3,
          "en": "The reason for this is that right now I'm checking",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 324.3,
          "end": 329.3,
          "en": "if control value is part of this array, this will return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 329.31,
          "end": 331.77,
          "en": "minus one if it is not part.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 331.77,
          "end": 334.14,
          "en": "Well minus one is interpreted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 334.14,
          "end": 335.94,
          "en": "as true though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 335.94,
          "end": 339.87,
          "en": "So we need to check if this is not equal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 339.87,
          "end": 341.46,
          "en": "to minus one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 341.46,
          "end": 344.7,
          "en": "So if this is not equal to minus one, that means we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 344.7,
          "end": 345.78,
          "en": "did find it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 345.78,
          "end": 347.46,
          "en": "That means it is invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 347.46,
          "end": 352.29,
          "en": "So now with this in place, if we go back, inspect this again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 352.29,
